// plugin/my_map.d.rut — the DECLARATION FILE for "plugin:my_map".
//
// `host` is a .d.rut-ONLY keyword (RFC 0029): a .rut file that spells it
// is a compile error. This file is pure surface — signatures, no bodies —
// and compiles to a DeclIr (.d.ir cache; version-locked, regenerable).
// rutc, the LSP, and AOT builds consume it with ZERO Rust linked (the tur
// index.d.ts role, in-language and type-checked). The Rust IMPLEMENTATION
// is the sibling file examples/host/my_map.rs, bound by name at embedder
// startup and proven signature-equal at vm.load link.
//
// Import specifiers map to declaration files by path: "plugin:my_map" ->
// plugin/my_map.d.rut. Only EXPORTED decls are nameable outside.
//
// There is no `host class` anymore: native state crosses as `Opaque` and
// RUT wraps it in a class (examples/host/my-map.rut — the `Logger`
// pattern, RFC 0028). Host fn signatures are CONCRETE over the crossing
// set (RFC 0023 §1): primitives, str, bytes, unit, Option/Result over
// those, Opaque — so a map's values cross as `Opaque` (the checked
// erasure of RFC 0014; `downcast<T>` recovers them) and keys are `str`
// (hashed host-side by content). Generic host state and admission-only
// bounds (`K requires Hashable`) went with `host class`: what crosses is
// exactly what the boundary can check.

// the instance handle — an Opaque box holding the Rust HashMap; the
// boxed value's Rust Drop runs when the box's rc hits 0 (RFC 0016 §5)
pub host fn my_map_new(cap: i32) -> Opaque;
pub host fn my_map_set(m: Opaque, k: str, v: Opaque) -> unit;
pub host fn my_map_get(m: Opaque, k: str) -> Option<Opaque>;   // None on a miss
pub host fn my_map_size(m: Opaque) -> i32;

// What compiling this file produces: a slot table
//     my_map_new -> 0, my_map_set -> 1, my_map_get -> 2, my_map_size -> 3
// (declaration order; part of the decl digest). Consumer calls compile
// to callnat { slot } — names are binding-time labels for the Rust impl,
// never dispatch keys, never in the IR (RFC 0032).
